INT. HALCYON HOUSE — BALLROOM — NIGHT

[[SHOT: WIDE — TRAVELLING]]

The ballroom: emerald walls, a brass bandstand, a floor so crowded the dancers move like one animal. The HOUSE BAND is in full swing.

[[TIME: 5]]
[[MUSIC: House band, full swing; carries the whole release.]]
[[ENTER: SLOANE]]
[[WARDROBE: SLOANE: WD-SLOANE-PARTY-GE92]]

Sloane moves through it like weather: a hand on a shoulder, a name remembered, a drink rescued, never quite stopping. She has a YOUNG PRODUCER by the elbow and is steering him toward the bar.

[[TIME: 5]]
[[ENTER: PRODUCER]]
[[ENTER: PIANIST]]

SLOANE
That piano loop you've built three albums on?

PRODUCER
Yeah?

She turns him to face a RETIRED JAZZ PIANIST holding court at the end of the bar.

[[TIME: 2]]

SLOANE
He's alive. Say hello.

[[REACTION: PRODUCER — Frozen, starstruck.]]

The pianist offers his hand, enjoying this enormously.

PIANIST
You cut the ninth out of my chord.

PRODUCER
It was crowding the bass.

PIANIST
It was holding the bass up.

PRODUCER
Then why does my version work?

PIANIST
Because you kept the eleventh. Sit down. I'll show you.

They lean in, already arguing, both delighted. Sloane backs away, leaving them to it.

[[TIME: 3]]
[[REACTION: SLOANE — Watching them argue about one chord, completely happy.]]
[[EXIT: PRODUCER]]
[[EXIT: PIANIST]]
[[ENTER: STRANGER]]

The band kicks into something faster. A STRANGER offers his hand. Sloane takes it without asking his name.

[[TIME: 3]]
[[SHOT: MEDIUM WIDE — CIRCLING]]

They dance a full chorus. She's good, really good, and so is he. The floor opens a little around them without anyone deciding to. On the last bar he spins her out, and she comes back on the beat.

[[TIME: 24]]
[[EXIT: STRANGER]]
[[ENTER: MAN IN THE ORANGE JACKET]]
[[WARDROBE: MAN IN THE ORANGE JACKET: WD-ORANGE-JACKET]]

Flushed and laughing, Sloane comes off the floor and passes a MAN IN A BOLD ORANGE JACKET. She doesn't stop.

[[TIME: 3]]

SLOANE
(lightly, passing)
Brave.

[[ENTER: GUESTS]]

Behind her, two GUESTS immediately lean in to read the label inside his collar. The man in the jacket stands very still and lets them.

[[TIME: 4]]
[[INSERT: Fingers turning back an orange collar to find the label.]]

Sloane glances back and sees it. Her smile holds a fraction too long.

[[TIME: 3]]
[[ENTER: GIDEON]]
[[WARDROBE: GIDEON: WD-GIDEON-SUIT]]

Gideon is at her elbow, the way he always is, and holds up the folded note between two fingers.

[[TIME: 3]]
[[PROP: PR-KAI-NOTE: held up between Gideon's fingers]]

SLOANE
Who's it from?

GIDEON
Not here.

She looks at the note, then at him, and the party noise seems to drop a little.

[[TIME: 3]]

CUT TO:
